<h1>Cookie policy</h1><p>Last updated: 22 August 2026</p><p>This page describes cookies and similar storage used by EmCP at <a href="https://emcp.m6i.it">emcp.m6i.it</a>. It sits next to the <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>, which covers personal data more broadly.</p><p>Controller: <strong>Antonio Molinari</strong>, Via Caselle 6, 26032 Ostiano (CR), Italy — <a href="mailto:support@m6i.it">support@m6i.it</a>.</p><h2>What a cookie is</h2><p>A cookie is a small piece of data a site can store on your device. Similar jobs can be done with local storage or with cookies set by other domains when the page loads their scripts. They can be strictly necessary for the service you asked for, or optional (statistics, advertising, extra features).</p><h2>What EmCP uses today</h2><p>EmCP currently uses <strong>technical storage only</strong>. There is no consent banner because there are no optional analytics, advertising, or profiling cookies. If that changes, this page will be updated and, where the law requires it, a choice will be offered before those tools run.</p><h3>Session cookie</h3><p>The application sets an encrypted session cookie (name in the form <code>_emcp_session</code>). It keeps you signed in, stores the CSRF token that protects forms, and remembers the interface language you selected. It is a first-party cookie, typically for the duration of the browser session, and is marked Secure in production.</p><p>Legal basis: it is needed to provide the service you request (login and a working site). Under the Italian ePrivacy rules, strictly necessary cookies of this kind do not require prior consent.</p><h3>Invitation cookie</h3><p>If you arrive with an invitation code, EmCP may set <code>emcp_invitation</code> so the code survives until you finish signing up. It is first-party and technical. You can drop it by clearing this site’s cookies.</p><h2>What is not used today</h2><p>At the date on this page EmCP does not use:</p><ul><li value="1">audience measurement or product analytics cookies;</li><li value="2">advertising, remarketing, or social pixels;</li><li value="3">session replay or heatmaps;</li><li value="4">a third-party consent platform;</li><li value="5">chat widgets that drop their own tracking cookies.</li></ul><p>Browser session replay and marketing error tags are not enabled.</p><h2>Third-party requests that are not EmCP cookies</h2><p>Some pages ask your browser to fetch resources from other hosts so the interface can render:</p><ul><li value="1"><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — web fonts. Google may see your IP address and user agent.</li><li value="2"><strong>Google Sign-In</strong> — if you sign in with Google, Google’s own cookies and storage apply on Google’s domains during that flow. EmCP does not control them.</li></ul><p>Those requests are there to show fonts or to complete login. They are not EmCP advertising tools. Details and transfer information are in the privacy policy.</p><h2>How to control cookies</h2><p>You can delete or block cookies in your browser settings. Blocking the session cookie will prevent sign-in and some forms from working. Clearing site data also removes the invitation cookie and any local preferences.</p><p>Browser help pages (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge) explain how to see which cookies a site has stored.</p><h2>Updates</h2><p>If optional cookies are introduced — for example to understand how the public landing is used, or because a paid checkout needs a payment provider’s script — this policy will list them, say whether they are first- or third-party, and wait for consent where required.</p>